From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: ListView multiple selection, SelectedItems, SelectionChanged; horizontal item panels

A ListView keeps a set of selected items now. In Multiple mode a click or Space toggles an item and the arrow keys leave the selection alone; in Extended mode a click or Down selects one item, Shift extends the range from where it started, Ctrl+click and Ctrl+Space toggle, and Ctrl+arrows move the focus alone. SelectedItems holds the selection and the list follows when the application adds or removes items there; SelectionChanged is raised with AddedItems and RemovedItems; SelectedIndex and SelectedItem are the first selected. An ItemsPanel that is a horizontal StackPanel, ItemsStackPanel or VirtualizingStackPanel lays the items out in a row, with Left and Right for the keyboard. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
